# Reviewing changes in `frontend/`

The unified reviewer (`prompts/codeReviewer/v3/`) loads **`frontend/REVIEW.md`** for any
changed path under `frontend/`. That map cites rule IDs from `frontend/AGENTS.md`
(FD1–FD7, FE-AP-4/6/7/12/18/19 auto-rejects) and `STYLE_GUIDE_FRONTEND.md` — it never
restates the rule text. This map **supersedes** the legacy
`prompts/codeReviewer/frontend/` and `prompts/codeReviewer/explainability_frontend/`
prompt families.

Deterministic TS predicates that fire here first (precedence over LLM), via
`code_reviewer/frontend/tools.py` → `code_reviewer/frontend/findings.py`:
- FD3 `check_csp_strict` — no `'unsafe-inline'`; rely on per-request nonce + `strict-dynamic`.
- FD3 `check_iframe_sandbox` — `sandbox="allow-scripts"` only.
- FD3 `check_secrets_in_public_env` — no `NEXT_PUBLIC_` secret-shaped values (FE-AP-18).
- FD3 `check_jwt_storage` — no JWT in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` (HttpOnly cookie).
- FD2 `check_composer_keyboard` — composer keyboard contract (U-family).

> Frontend TS tools require `tsx` (`cd frontend && npm install`). Missing `tsx` surfaces
> as a `gaps[]` entry, not a hard failure.

Dispatch the reviewer:

```bash
python -m meta.code_reviewer --from-git-diff --git-base HEAD --prompt-version v3 --output review.json
```

Deterministic findings are the gate; the v3 LLM judge is WI-8 certified (TPR/TNR = 1.0) so LLM verdicts are gate-grade for the routed LLM-only rules — re-record when the judge model changes.
Full contract: `docs/skills/code-review/SKILL.md`.
